;;; A bare `_` as a fact's argument is dropped at load, in silence —
;;; **W29**, regression `fact-arg` (`corpus/regressions.toml`),
;;; under Q-M1e2.22.
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A relation of two arguments and two facts over it, the first writing the
;;; bare `_` as its first argument.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A bare `_` is reserved and names nothing (Q-M1e2.22), so the program is
;;; refused at load, with a line naming the place: every command that reads
;;; it exits 1 (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered, and what it answers ──────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `ec004a48` (the engine `916d97ac`'s), release and debug alike: the
;;; loader dropped the `_` and stored the one-argument `(r a)` beside `(r a
;;; b)`, against a two-argument declaration, with no line. Root's state was
;;; `(model (r a b) (r a))` and R two states, exit 0 (`ein solve FILE`, `ein
;;; oracle FILE`). Today the parse refuses the `_`.

(relation r T T)
(r _ a)
(r a b)
